/* Distinguishes an actual food ingredient from a raw material that is
   never food - packaging, labels, cleaning supplies, etc. Without this,
   a packaging component sitting in a finished product's BOM (a box, a
   wrapper) gets flattened right alongside real food ingredients and
   shows up in the printed ingredient list and nutrition panel, which is
   wrong - packaging is never a food ingredient under FIC.

   Free text, not a DB-enforced enum (matching nutData.item_nut_cfg's
   placement values) - a client can add more categories later (e.g.
   "CLEANING", "PROCESSING_AID") without a schema change, since
   IngredientLabelEngine.flattenRecursive only ever tests for FOOD and
   treats anything else the same way (excluded from ingredient lists and
   nutrition rollups).

   Single-shot ALTER TABLE (not safely re-runnable), same convention as
   .patchsqlv_ingredientlabeling's storage/usage-instruction columns.
*/
alter table ing_mstr add column ing_material_type varchar(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'FOOD';
